	"notes": [
		{
			"id": "AKYhEueGd54sZG9lI",
			"text": "Typical Stats from the reviewed package: ST 5, DX 11, IQ 3, HT 10, HP 5, WILL 10, PER 10, FP 10, SPEED 5.25, MOVE 3, DODGE 8, DR —. GCS derives its own values by applying the ancestry; where the two differ, the package's Typical Stats are what the Dungeons on Automatic encounter tables use."
		},
		{
			"id": "ADJA3-nG-XvaYC9jd",
			"text": "Encounter rating: CER 3 (offense 8, protection -5), threat tier minor, appearing 6."
		},
		{
			"id": "A0nQluZfUTnsN_OZ4",
			"text": "Petrification, reach C: With a Ready maneuver, a cockatrice can activate its petrification ability. Any creature that touches the cockatrice, even insubstantial or ethereal creatures, must make an HT roll to resist. If it fails, then the creature becomes permanently petrified. This effect cannot be dispelled by Dispel Magic, but can be negated by Remove Curse or Stone to Flesh. This ability stays on until the cockatrice turns it off with a Ready maneuver, and it works even if it is stunned, unconscious, or asleep, but not dead (however, the tail feathers retain this ability 1d days after death). Cockatrices are immune to this petrification ability, but not to other petrification effects."
		},
		{
			"id": "AsqoMinqGAZFtGcH9",
			"text": "GCS ancestry draft: gcs/cockatrice.gct"
		},
